### TomoFlix server — manual request collection.
### Run the server first: `docker compose up --build` (or `go run .` in
### server/), then fire these with an HTTP client that understands the
### `###`-delimited .http format (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains HTTP Client).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check — happy path
# Expect: 200 OK, body "ok"
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Local media — happy path (full file)
# Expect: 200 OK, Content-Type based on file extension (video or audio),
# full file body. Replace sample.mp4 with a real file in TOMOFLIX_MEDIA_DIR.
GET {{baseUrl}}/stream/local/sample.mp4

### Local media — happy path (range request, e.g. seeking)
# Expect: 206 Partial Content, Content-Range header, only the requested
# byte range in the body.
GET {{baseUrl}}/stream/local/sample.mp4
Range: bytes=0-1023

### Local media — error case: file does not exist
# Expect: 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/stream/local/does-not-exist.mp4

### Local media — error case: no filename given
# Expect: 400 Bad Request, body "no file specified"
GET {{baseUrl}}/stream/local/
